[c-LoD] c-LoD v6.9.2: STAGE EYES v2 — run #231 measured rot=ok scan=15 lens_zero=1 while the carrier column is PLAINLY VISIBLE on the burst shot (4268 green px) and the relative strobe arm fires on 399/400 of the actual dot pixels — the hue test and the camera decode are INNOCENT; the residual suspects are the projection INPUTS. The four lens strips become bucket printers: CAM (the Globals CameraBlockPos the capture sees, in cell-space buckets over the atlas — a wrong bucket convicts the post-chain camera), ROT (az/el buckets from clod_rot_a), HITS (clod_h_b.g strobe-fired cells on a 32x32 grid), MASK (clod_mask marks on a dense 64x36 grid — v6.9.0 32x18 could miss 2-3px discs). The RENDERER DEAD marker decodes the buckets against the known vantage (cam ~8, az ~0 east, el ~3) and names: Globals-camera-wrong vs az-wrong vs strobe-never-fires vs merge-dead. Also #231 taught: the visible column survives the eraser because a DENSE column repaint copies dot colors from dot neighbors (the self-repairing fill assumed isolated dots) — cosmetic, noted. v6.9.1 carried: numpy CI deps, the dynamic prompt click + prompt guard
